From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:35:49 -0400
Subject: little: links from other apps open in a small window

A link handed over by another application opens a popup-type window
marked as Stedding's little window, centred over the last-active window
(1000 x 700 at most), unless a route names a Space for it (the route
wins) or the setting is off (then a tab, in the Space for links from
other apps). Inside it, cmd-O sends the page, the same WebContents, into
the last-active window's active Space, shift-cmd-O into a split with its
active tab, ctrl-1..9 into Space N, and Escape closes it; the bar lists
"Open in <Space>" for each Space. A little window archives after its own
idle (6 hours against 12) by closing into the recently-closed list. The
command ids stay out of chrome_command_ids.h (docs/features/little.md
E1-E5; E1's bar is Chromium's popup bar in this cut).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 4, R6-30: Little Arc.
Removable when: Chromium opens external links in a transient window of
its own.
